### Install PHPStan extensions via Composer

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan/blob/2.2.x/website/src/user-guide/extension-library.md

Use the extension-installer plugin to automatically enable extensions upon installation.

```bash
composer require --dev phpstan/extension-installer && \
composer require --dev phpstan/phpstan-beberlei-assert
```

--------------------------------

### Manually include extension configuration

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan/blob/2.2.x/website/src/user-guide/extension-library.md

Include specific extension files in the includes section of the configuration when granular control is required.

```yaml
includes:
	- vendor/phpstan/phpstan-beberlei-assert/extension.neon
```

--------------------------------

### Additional Config Files Format

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan/blob/2.2.x/website/src/_posts/upgrading-from-phpstan-1-to-2.md

The 'additionalConfigFiles' parameter in PHPStan configuration must now be a list.

```neon
parameters:
	additionalConfigFiles:
		- phpstan-baseline.neon
		- phpstan-ci.neon
```

--------------------------------

### ContainerFactory getConfigFiles() — includes from decoded data

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan/blob/2.2.x/phpstan.phar

PHPStan reads `includes` from the already-decoded NEON array (`$data['includes']`), not from raw text. The NEON parser (Lexer + Parser) has already handled all syntactic variations — quoted keys, inline `[]` arrays, multiline strings, comments — before this code runs. Line-based grep on the raw `.neon` file is fundamentally unreliable for detecting settings because the parser strips comments, normalizes whitespace, and resolves indentation before `includes` is ever accessed.

```php
private static function getConfigFiles(FileHelper $fileHelper, \PHPStan\DependencyInjection\NeonCachedFileReader $neonAdapter, PhpAdapter $phpAdapter, string $configFile, array $loaderParameters, ?string $generateBaselineFile): array
    {
        if ($generateBaselineFile === $fileHelper->normalizePath($configFile)) {
            return [[], []];
        }
        if (!is_file($configFile) || !is_readable($configFile)) {
            return [[], []];
        }
        if (str_ends_with($configFile, '.php')) {
            $data = $phpAdapter->load($configFile);
        } else {
            $data = $neonAdapter->load($configFile);
        }
        $allConfigFiles = [$configFile];
        if (isset($data['includes'])) {
            Validators::assert($data['includes'], 'list', sprintf("section 'includes' in file '%s'", $configFile));
            $includes = Helpers::expand($data['includes'], $loaderParameters);
            foreach ($includes as $include) {
                $include = self::expandIncludedFile($include, $configFile);
                [$tmpConfigFiles, $tmpConfigArray] = self::getConfigFiles($fileHelper, $neonAdapter, $phpAdapter, $include, $loaderParameters, $generateBaselineFile);
                $allConfigFiles = array_merge($allConfigFiles, $tmpConfigFiles);
                $data = \Nette\Schema\Helpers::merge($tmpConfigArray, $data);
            }
        }
        return [$allConfigFiles, $data];
    }
```

### Extension Library > Installing extensions

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan/blob/2.2.x/website/src/user-guide/extension-library.md

Extensions can be installed using the phpstan/extension-installer Composer plugin, which automatically enables them upon installation. If granular control is required—such as enabling only specific rules or configuration files from an extension—users should manually include the extension's configuration file in the includes section of their PHPStan configuration.

